   $q$An infinite geometric series has first term $12$ and sum $30$. What is its common ratio $r$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{3}{5}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{5}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-sum-by-first-term"},{"text":"$-\\frac{3}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-solving-for-r"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-one-minus-r"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{3}{5}$$q$, $q$A finite sum requires $|r| < 1$ and then $\frac{12}{1 - r} = 30$. So $1 - r = \frac{12}{30} = \frac{2}{5}$, giving $r = \frac{3}{5}$. Check: $\frac{12}{1 - \frac{3}{5}} = \frac{12}{\frac{2}{5}} = 30$. The choice $\frac{2}{5}$ is the value of $1 - r$, not $r$.$q$, 'draft', null)
