   $q$A ball is dropped from a height of $10$ feet. After each bounce it rises to $\frac{3}{5}$ of the height it just fell, and it keeps bouncing forever in this model. What is the total vertical distance, in feet, the ball travels (all falls and all rises)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$40$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$50$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"doubled-the-first-drop-too"},{"text":"$15$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"counted-only-the-rises"},{"text":"$25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"counted-only-the-falls"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$40$$q$, $q$The falls are $10 + 6 + 3.6 + \dots$, an infinite geometric series with $r = \frac{3}{5}$ and $|r| < 1$, so they total $\frac{10}{1 - \frac{3}{5}} = 25$. The rises are $6 + 3.6 + \dots = \frac{6}{1 - \frac{3}{5}} = 15$. Together the ball travels $25 + 15 = 40$ feet. The value $50$ doubles every fall, but the first $10$-foot drop has no matching rise before it.$q$, 'draft', null)
